    {id:"cardio",title:"Conditioning for athletes",
     summary:"Endurance athletes typically do about 80% of sessions at easy, conversational intensity and around 20% as hard intervals near maximal aerobic effort. Both continuous and interval training raise VO2max substantially, and intervals get there in less time. If you also lift, keep hard running away from heavy leg days and separate sessions by a few hours, since interference shows up mainly with running and high cardio volumes.",
     points:["About 80% easy aerobic work, 20% hard","1–2 interval sessions a week, the rest easy","Separate lifting and hard cardio by 3+ hours","Cycling may interfere less with leg gains than running"],
     links:[
      {t:"Training intensity distribution in endurance athletes — IJSPP",u:"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20861519/",k:"study",d:"Seiler on the 80/20 pattern of elite athletes"},
      {t:"Interval vs continuous training for VO2max — Sports Medicine",u:"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26243014/",k:"study",d:"Both raise VO2max; intervals slightly more"},
      {t:"Compatibility of concurrent training meta-analysis — Sports Medicine",u:"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8891239/",k:"study",d:"Cardio mainly blunts explosive strength, if same-session"},
      {t:"Concurrent training interference meta-analysis — J Strength Cond Res",u:"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22002517/",k:"study",d:"Running, frequency and duration drive interference"},
      {t:"Concurrent training for the powerlifter — Stronger By Science",u:"https://www.strongerbyscience.com/concurrent-training/",k:"article",d:"How strength athletes can add cardio wisely"}]},
    {id:"sprint",title:"Sprinting & speed: short, fast and fully rested",summary:"Sprint coaches build speed by running fast often, in small doses, with full recovery. Tony Holler's Feed the Cats gives sprinters a few timed flying runs, never more than 200 m in practice, and posts every time; Charlie Francis split the week into high days, when sprints, jumps and heavy lifts are stacked together, and low days of easy tempo running. Glen Mills rebuilt Usain Bolt's posture and core strength after linking his recurring hamstring trouble to poor mechanics, and Dan Pfaff asks why an exercise is there before he chooses it. Bolt, Mills and Jamaica's sprint culture are covered under World → Jamaica.",points:["Drills first, then about three timed flying 10–20 m runs","Full rest and few reps, so every run is fast","Sprint no more than three days a week","High days stack speed, jumps and heavy lifts; low days stay under 75%","Time every rep, then record, rank and publish it","Top speed lasts about 50–60 m; hold stride length after"],exercises:["High knees","Stride-outs","Sprints","Standing long jump","Squats","Bench press","Tempo runs","Push ups","Sit-ups"],days:[{name:"Feed the Cats speed day",note:"Drills, then three timed flying 10s or 20s, full rest",ex:["High knees","Stride-outs","Sprints"]},{name:"Francis high day",note:"Sprints, jumps and heavy lifts on the same day",ex:["Sprints","Standing long jump","Squats","Bench press"]},{name:"Francis low day",note:"Tempo runs on grass below 75% speed, then a light circuit",ex:["Tempo runs","Push ups","Sit-ups"]}],links:[{t:"Maximum velocity training: Tony Holler and Feed the Cats — SimpliFaster",u:"https://simplifaster.com/articles/holler-maximum-velocity/",k:"article",d:"Flying sprints, record-rank-publish and his low-volume season"},{t:"Bigger Faster Stronger meets Feed the Cats — Just Fly Performance Podcast",u:"https://www.just-fly-sports.com/podcast-135-tony-holler/",k:"podcast",d:"Holler on high school sprinters and the weight room"},{t:"Charlie Francis archives — CharlieFrancis.com",u:"https://www.charliefrancis.com/",k:"article",d:"His books, video series and training writings"},{t:"The Structure of Training for Speed — CharlieFrancis.com",u:"https://www.charliefrancis.com/products/the-structure-of-training-for-speed-e-book",k:"article",d:"His key-concepts e-book on organising speed training"},{t:"Revisiting the high-low concept of training — Derek Hansen",u:"https://www.sprintcoach.com/blog/revisiting-the-high-low-concept-of-training",k:"article",d:"Defining and refining Francis's high-low week"},{t:"Ben Johnson on the Toronto Legends Podcast",u:"https://www.torontolegends.ca/ben-johnson-icymi/",k:"podcast",d:"Johnson on Charlie Francis and his Seoul 100 m"},{t:"Charlie Francis biography — Wikipedia",u:"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlie_Francis",k:"article",d:"His sprinting career, athletes and coaching"},{t:"Glen Mills interview — New Studies in Athletics (World Athletics)",u:"https://worldathletics.org/download/downloadnsa?filename=99a6b7b6-3d3b-4f7e-ae6d-1f8aeecbdc9e.pdf&urlslug=nsa-interview-glen-mills",k:"article",d:"Mills on Bolt's posture, core and strength work"},{t:"Dan Pfaff on why it depends — SimpliFaster",u:"https://simplifaster.com/articles/episode-45-dan-pfaff/",k:"article",d:"Pfaff on lifting, cueing and stretching for speed"},{t:"Dan Pfaff (#87) — Pacey Performance Podcast",u:"https://paceyperformancepodcast.podbean.com/e/pacey-performance-podcast-87-dan-pfaff/",k:"podcast",d:"The ALTIS coach on his career and 400 m training"},{t:"Coaching sprint technique with large teams — Dan Pfaff (YouTube)",u:"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=prxpbXc5u0c",k:"video",d:"Pfaff on teaching sprint mechanics to groups"},{t:"Speed truth, part 1 — Ben Patrick",u:"https://kneesovertoesguy.substack.com/p/atg-speed-truth-part-1",k:"article",d:"Shin angle, deep knee strength and acceleration"},{t:"The training and development of elite sprint performance — Sports Medicine Open",u:"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6872694/",k:"study",d:"Joins coaches' best practice with sprint research"},{t:"Resisted-sprint training and load meta-analysis — Scand J Med Sci Sports",u:"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41384676/",k:"study",d:"Very heavy sleds sharpened trained sprinters' first five metres"}],related:["jm-mills","jm-bolt"]},
    {id:"plyo",title:"Plyometrics & jumping: react fast, land soft",summary:"Plyometrics train the quick stretch and rebound of muscle and tendon that sprinting and jumping depend on. Kelly Baggett, who added about 20 inches to his own vertical, separates reactive skill from the strength behind it and assesses the hips, knees and ankles in turn; Joel Smith of Just Fly Sports keeps two to four jump drills in a programme at a time, done with full intent alongside sprinting and lifting. Ben Patrick, nowhere near dunking at 20, got there by first rebuilding his knees with backward walking, backward step-ups, deep split squats and deep squats. The depth jump itself comes from Yuri Verkhoshansky's shock method, covered under World → Russia.",points:["Two to four jump drills at a time; rotate every 3–8 weeks","Full intent on every jump; plyos support sprinting and lifting","Usable strength for jumpers: about a double-bodyweight squat","A standing triple jump over 30 ft is a solid mark","Find whether hips, knees or ankles lag, then train that link","Fewer jumps after 30, but keep sprinting"],exercises:["Box jumps","Depth jump","Standing long jump","Trap bar deadlift","Squats","Bulgarian split squat","Backward sled drag","Backward step-up","ATG split squat","ATG squat"],days:[{name:"Jump and lift day",note:"Two to four jump drills at full intent, then basic lifts",ex:["Box jumps","Depth jump","Standing long jump","Trap bar deadlift","Bulgarian split squat"]},{name:"Patrick's dunk foundation",note:"Backward walking, step-ups and split squats, then deep squats",ex:["Backward sled drag","Backward step-up","ATG split squat","ATG squat"]}],links:[,{t:"The Vertical Jump Development Bible — Goodreads",u:"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/7193769-the-vertical-jump-development-bible",k:"article",d:"Baggett's jump book with test-based programmes"},{t:"How to jump higher: the Joel Smith Q&A — SimpliFaster",u:"https://simplifaster.com/articles/joel-smith-how-to-jump-higher/",k:"article",d:"Splits, jumper standards and how many plyos to run"},{t:"Solo AMT depth jumps — Just Fly Sports",u:"https://www.just-fly-sports.com/potw-11-solo-amt-depth-jumps/",k:"article",d:"A depth-jump variation from his plyometric series"},{t:"Rapid vertical jump improvement — Just Fly Sports",u:"https://www.just-fly-sports.com/rapid-vertical-jump-improvement/",k:"article",d:"Quick ways to raise your jump"},{t:"How to get your first dunk — Ben Patrick",u:"https://kneesovertoesguy.substack.com/p/how-to-get-your-first-dunk",k:"article",d:"His knee-first route from no dunk to dunking"},{t:"Ben Patrick on building bulletproof knees — Just Fly Performance Podcast",u:"https://www.just-fly-sports.com/podcast-148-ben-patrick/",k:"podcast",d:"Knee resilience and jumping, with Joel Smith"},{t:"Official channel — Isaiah Rivera (YouTube)",u:"https://www.youtube.com/@IsaiahRivera1",k:"video",d:"Jump training from a record-holding pro dunker"},{t:"Dunk wisdom with Isaiah Rivera (#36) — Jacked Athlete",u:"https://jackedathlete.com/podcast-36-dunk-wisdom-with-isaiah-rivera/",k:"podcast",d:"Rivera on training for the dunk"},{t:"Does plyometric training improve vertical jump height? — Br J Sports Med",u:"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17347316/",k:"study",d:"Plyometrics raised jump height by about 5–9%"},{t:"Effects of plyometric training: an umbrella review — Sports Medicine Open",u:"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9832201/",k:"study",d:"Plyometrics improve most fitness and sport measures"}],related:["su-verkhoshansky"]},
    {id:"strongman",title:"Strongman training: lifts first, then the events",summary:"Strongman competitors build a base with the barbell and then carry, load and press awkward objects: the yoke, farmer's handles, the log and Atlas stones. Brian Shaw, Hafþór Björnsson and Eddie Hall share their own training on their channels, and coach Matt Mills's 16-week beginner plan puts an event or two into each of four lifting days, starting the first week at an easy RPE 6. Shannon Green, writing on 70's Big, finds the yoke the most draining event and usually leaves stones until the end of a session. Strongman's history and its Nordic champions are covered under World → Nordic & Celtic.",points:["Get strong on the barbell before heavy event work","Beginners start events around RPE 6 and add a little weekly","Yoke 3×60 ft, farmers 2×60 ft, stones 2×6–8","Stones usually go last; heavy stones need tacky","Deload in the middle of a 16-week block","Implements carry more injury risk, so build up gradually"],exercises:["Log press","Bench press","T-bar row","Lat pulldown","Cable bicep curl","Cable tricep pushdown","Seated leg curl","Safety bar squat","Yoke carry","Bulgarian split squat","Ab wheel rollout","Deadlift","Farmer carry","Atlas stone lift","Pull ups","Hanging leg raise"],days:[{name:"Log day",note:"Log clean and press 3×6–8, then accessories",ex:["Log press","Bench press","T-bar row","Lat pulldown","Cable bicep curl","Cable tricep pushdown"]},{name:"Squat and yoke day",note:"Yoke 3×60 ft, starting around RPE 6",ex:["Seated leg curl","Safety bar squat","Yoke carry","Bulgarian split squat","Ab wheel rollout"]},{name:"Deadlift and events day",note:"Deadlift 3×5, farmers 2×60 ft, stones 2×6–8",ex:["Deadlift","Farmer carry","Atlas stone lift","Pull ups","Hanging leg raise"]}],links:[{t:"Official channel — Brian Shaw (SHAWSTRENGTH, YouTube)",u:"https://www.youtube.com/@shawstrength",k:"video",d:"Training, events and eating from the four-time champion"},{t:"Shaw Strength — Brian Shaw",u:"https://www.shawstrength.com/",k:"article",d:"His site, programmes and Strongest Man on Earth contest"},{t:"Official channel — Hafþór Björnsson (YouTube)",u:"https://www.youtube.com/@Hafthorjulius",k:"video",d:"The Mountain's training sessions and contest preparation"},{t:"Deadlift session, episode 5 — Hafþór Björnsson (YouTube)",u:"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vw6RfGSvzbo",k:"video",d:"A full deadlift workout with Björnsson"},{t:"Official channel — Eddie Hall (YouTube)",u:"https://www.youtube.com/@EddieHallWSM",k:"video",d:"The 2017 champion's training and strength challenges"},{t:"The Good, The Bad & The Beast — Eddie Hall (Spotify)",u:"https://open.spotify.com/show/70uKjStd2m28MlaVI7yAQp",k:"podcast",d:"Hall's conversations with elite strength athletes"},{t:"World's Strongest Man Podcast — Audioboom",u:"https://audioboom.com/channels/4878275-world-s-strongest-man-podcast",k:"podcast",d:"Athlete interviews around the World's Strongest Man"},{t:"The beginner strongman program — Matt Mills (EliteFTS)",u:"https://elitefts.com/blogs/training/beginner-strongman-program",k:"article",d:"Sixteen weeks, four days, events added gradually"},{t:"Strongman programming with Shannon Green — 70's Big",u:"https://70sbig.com/blog/2012/02/strongman-programming/",k:"article",d:"Two templates for mixing events and barbell work"},{t:"Strongman training for beginners — 70's Big",u:"https://70sbig.com/blog/2011/12/strongman-training-for-beginners/",k:"article",d:"Shannon Green on starting out with implements"},{t:"Strongman vs traditional resistance training — J Strength Cond Res",u:"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25627449/",k:"study",d:"Seven weeks of strongman matched traditional training overall"},{t:"The biomechanics and applications of strongman exercises — Sports Medicine Open",u:"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6901656/",k:"study",d:"What's known about yoke, farmers, log and stone mechanics"},{t:"Injury epidemiology of strongman athletes — J Strength Cond Res",u:"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23669816/",k:"study",d:"Implement training carried 1.9 times the injury risk"}],related:["nc-wsm","nc-carries","nc-stones"]},
    {id:"oly",title:"Olympic weightlifting: position, movement, speed, load",summary:"The snatch and the clean and jerk are fast, technical lifts, and their coaches build them in a set order. Greg Everett of Catalyst Athletics teaches position first, then movement, then speed, and adds load last, using slower partial drills such as the muscle snatch on the way; Glenn Pendlay kept programmes simple, stayed at triples or fewer in the competition lifts, and used timed singles every minute. Ukrainian lifter and coach Oleksiy Torokhtiy and Athens 2004 champion Zhang Guozheng show the lifts at full speed on video. The Chinese and Bulgarian systems are covered under World → China and World → Bulgaria.",points:["Learn in order: position, movement, speed, then load","Hold start and catch positions a few seconds while learning","No more than triples in the snatch and clean and jerk","Timed sets: a snatch single every minute for 10 at about 70%","Gather work above 80%; save max attempts for late in the week","Keep a log and change one thing at a time"],exercises:["Snatch","Power snatch","Hang snatch","Snatch pull","Overhead squat","Clean and jerk","Power clean","Jerk","Clean pull","Front squat","Squats","Push press"],days:[{name:"Snatch day",note:"Singles every minute, then pulls and front squats",ex:["Snatch","Snatch pull","Front squat"]},{name:"Clean and jerk day",note:"Doubles or triples above 80%, then pulls and squats",ex:["Clean and jerk","Clean pull","Squats"]},{name:"Technique and power day",note:"Lighter partial lifts; position before load",ex:["Power snatch","Hang snatch","Overhead squat","Power clean","Jerk","Push press"]}],links:[{t:"Hierarchy for learning the snatch and clean & jerk — Greg Everett (Catalyst Athletics)",u:"https://www.catalystathletics.com/article/2220/Hierarchy-for-Learning-the-Snatch-and-Clean-Jerk/",k:"article",d:"His order of priorities: position, movement, speed, load"},{t:"The power snatch: uses & cautions — Greg Everett (Catalyst Athletics)",u:"https://www.catalystathletics.com/article/126/The-Power-Snatch-Uses-Cautions/",k:"article",d:"Why he starts teaching the snatch with it"},{t:"Top 5 assistance exercises for the snatch — Greg Everett (Catalyst Athletics)",u:"https://www.catalystathletics.com/article/1900/Top-5-Assistance-Exercises-for-the-Snatch/",k:"article",d:"Tall snatches and other drills for the turnover"},{t:"Instructional weightlifting content — Catalyst Athletics",u:"https://www.catalystathletics.com/learn/",k:"article",d:"Technique articles, videos and an exercise library"},{t:"Podcasts with Greg Everett — Catalyst Athletics",u:"https://catalystathletics.com/article/1894/Podcasts-with-Greg-Everett",k:"podcast",d:"His interviews on coaching and the sport"},{t:"Official channel — Catalyst Athletics (YouTube)",u:"https://www.youtube.com/@CatalystAthletics",k:"video",d:"Technique tutorials and training footage"},{t:"Timed sets — Glenn Pendlay (StrongFirst)",u:"https://www.strongfirst.com/timed-sets/",k:"article",d:"His every-minute singles, from American Weightlifting"},{t:"Glenn Pendlay Q&A — 70's Big Podcast",u:"https://70sbig.com/blog/2011/10/podcast-9-glenn-pendlay-qa/",k:"podcast",d:"Pendlay answers readers on the lifts and programming"},{t:"Glenn Pendlay biography — Wikipedia",u:"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glenn_Pendlay",k:"article",d:"Coach of national champions; founded Wichita Falls Weightlifting"},{t:"Snatch: how to, benefits and variations — Oleksiy Torokhtiy",u:"https://store.torokhtiy.com/blogs/exercises/snatch-exercise",k:"article",d:"Torokhtiy's step-by-step guide to the snatch"},{t:"Official channel — Oleksiy Torokhtiy (YouTube)",u:"https://www.youtube.com/@torokhtiy",k:"video",d:"Technique fixes and programmes from the Ukrainian lifter"},{t:"Chinese weightlifting training with Zhang Guozheng — YouTube",u:"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BEtJGARoXgU",k:"video",d:"Chinese training hall, including his 200 kg clean and jerk"},{t:"Zhang Guozheng's life story — All Things Gym",u:"https://www.allthingsgym.com/chinese-weightlifting-documentary-zhang-guozhengs-life-story/",k:"video",d:"Documentary on the 2004 Olympic champion"},{t:"Olympic weightlifting training and vertical jump — Br J Sports Med",u:"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26626268/",k:"study",d:"Weightlifting raised jump height 7.7% versus no training"},{t:"Weightlifting vs traditional training vs plyometrics — Sports Medicine",u:"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9213388/",k:"study",d:"Weightlifting beat traditional lifting for jumps and power"}],related:["cn-weightlifting","bg-method"]},
    {id:"grip",title:"Grip & forearms: crush, pinch and hold",summary:"Grip specialists train the hand in separate ways: crushing with grippers, pinching plates, holding heavy or thick handles, and working the wrist. John Brookfield's Mastery of Hand Strength, published by IronMind, helped revive the field, and IronMind has certified closes of its Captains of Crush grippers since Richard Sorin closed the No. 3 in 1991. David Horne runs the World of Grip contests and has set a two-hands pinch world record, and Jedd Johnson of the Diesel Crew warns that most people do too much too soon, before their hands are ready.",points:["Train crush, pinch, support and wrist separately","Start easy; hands and tendons need time to adapt","Hold two crossed dumbbells in one hand to curl or row","Carries and thick bars build the holding grip","Gripper certification follows IronMind's official closing rules","Grip strength tracks long-term health in large studies"],exercises:["Gripper closes","Plate pinch","Wrist roller","Reverse curl","Farmer carry","Axle deadlift","Rope hang","Hammer curl","Wrist curl","Reverse wrist curl"],days:[{name:"Crush and pinch day",note:"Grippers, plate pinches and wrist work",ex:["Gripper closes","Plate pinch","Wrist roller","Reverse curl"]},{name:"Support grip day",note:"Heavy holds, a thick bar and two-dumbbell hammer curls",ex:["Farmer carry","Axle deadlift","Rope hang","Hammer curl"]}],links:[{t:"John Brookfield's grip tips — IronMind",u:"https://ironmind.com/articles/john-brookfields-grip-tips/",k:"article",d:"His two-dumbbell curls and other grip drills"},{t:"Stick to it — John Brookfield (IronMind)",u:"https://ironmind.com/articles/john-brookfields-grip-tips/Stick-to-It/",k:"article",d:"A plate-and-stick drill for grip and pulling"},{t:"Mastery of Hand Strength — Goodreads",u:"https://www.goodreads.com/en/book/show/2491676.Mastery_of_Hand_Strength",k:"article",d:"Brookfield's book on building hand strength"},{t:"Captains of Crush certification: the challenge — IronMind",u:"https://ironmind.com/news/Captains-of-Crush-Gripper-Certification-The-Challenge/",k:"article",d:"Gripper certification since Richard Sorin's 1991 close"},{t:"Captains of Crush rules for closing & certification — IronMind",u:"https://ironmind.com/product-info/certification/captains-of-crush/rules-for-closing-certification/",k:"article",d:"How official gripper closes are done and verified"},{t:"Who's who: No. 4 Captains of Crush — IronMind",u:"https://ironmind.com/product-info/certification/captains-of-crush/whos-who-no.-4-coc/",k:"article",d:"Everyone certified on the hardest gripper"},{t:"David Horne's World of Grip",u:"https://www.davidhorne-gripmaster.com/",k:"article",d:"Horne's articles, history and grip contests"},{t:"David Horne World of Grip interview — SoundCloud",u:"https://soundcloud.com/thecommandotemple/david-world-of-grip-interview",k:"podcast",d:"Horne talks grip training and competition"},{t:"David Horne breaks pinch grip world record — IronMind",u:"https://ironmind.com/news/David-Horne-Breaks-Pinch-Grip-World-Record",k:"article",d:"His record two-hands pinch lift"},{t:"Official channel — Jedd Johnson (YouTube)",u:"https://www.youtube.com/@gripstrength",k:"video",d:"Grip training, contests and feats from the Diesel Crew"},{t:"Get a grip: interview with Jedd Johnson — Power Athlete",u:"https://powerathletehq.com/get-grip/",k:"article",d:"Lift, hold and control: grip for athletes"},{t:"Gripper training articles — Diesel Crew",u:"https://www.dieselcrew.com/category/gripper-training/",k:"article",d:"Johnson's articles on training with grippers"},{t:"The Grip Authority — Jedd Johnson",u:"https://www.thegripauthority.com/",k:"article",d:"His grip-training membership site and programmes"},{t:"Prognostic value of grip strength (PURE) — The Lancet",u:"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25982160/",k:"study",d:"Weaker grip predicted higher death and heart-disease risk"},{t:"Grip strength in climbers vs other athletes — Int J Environ Res Public Health",u:"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7796164/",k:"study",d:"Climbers gripped harder, with less side-to-side difference"}]},
    {id:"combat",title:"Conditioning for combat sports: aerobic base, explosive finish",summary:"Fights run in rounds of three to five minutes with a minute's rest, so fighters need an aerobic engine to recover and the power to finish late. Joel Jamieson of 8 Weeks Out, author of Ultimate MMA Conditioning, tests each fighter and builds whichever side is lacking, often starting with long, steady cardiac-output work at 120–150 beats a minute; Phil Daru, coach to UFC fighters, stresses assessment, strength and breath work for grapplers. Wrestling and jiu-jitsu bring their own traditions: Dan Gable's rule to do what matters every day, and Rickson Gracie's breathing, sand and sea work, covered under World → USA and World → Brazil, with the zurkhaneh and chidaoba under World → Iran and World → Caucasus.",points:["Cardiac output: 30–90 minutes steady at 120–150 bpm","Cardiac power intervals: 2–3 min hard, 3–4 min easy","Assess first, then build the weaker energy system","Power-endurance: stay explosive into the late rounds","Basic lifts for strength; specific drills nearer the fight","If it's important, do it every day"],exercises:["Running","Cycling","Jump rope","Shadow boxing","Heavy bag","Sled drag","Kettlebell swings","Trap bar deadlift","Front squat","Pull ups","Rope climb","Farmer carry"],days:[{name:"Cardiac output session",note:"30–90 minutes steady at 120–150 beats a minute",ex:["Running","Cycling","Jump rope","Shadow boxing"]},{name:"Cardiac power intervals",note:"2–3 minutes up to max heart rate, 3–4 minutes easy",ex:["Heavy bag","Sled drag","Kettlebell swings"]},{name:"Fighter's strength day",note:"Basic lifts, then rope climbs and carries for grip",ex:["Trap bar deadlift","Front squat","Pull ups","Rope climb","Farmer carry"]}],links:[{t:"8 Weeks Out — Joel Jamieson",u:"https://8weeksout.com/",k:"article",d:"His articles on energy systems, HRV and fighters"},{t:"Explosive MMA conditioning — 8 Weeks Out",u:"https://8weeksout.com/2008/10/06/explosive-mma-conditioning/",k:"article",d:"Jamieson's plan for short, explosive power in fighters"},{t:"Truth about energy systems, day 3 — 8 Weeks Out",u:"https://8weeksout.com/truth-about-energy-systems-day-3/",k:"article",d:"Principles and methods for aerobic training"},{t:"Ultimate MMA Conditioning — 8 Weeks Out",u:"https://8weeksout.com/ultimate-mma-conditioning-order/",k:"article",d:"His book on conditioning methods for fighters"},{t:"Joel Jamieson interview — Robertson Training Systems",u:"https://robertsontrainingsystems.com/blog/joel-jamieson-interview/",k:"article",d:"Aerobic work, cardiac power intervals and fighters' problems"},{t:"Interview with MMA trainer Joel Jamieson — Bret Contreras",u:"https://bretcontreras.com/interview-with-mma-trainer-joel-jamieson/",k:"article",d:"Power-endurance, assessment and the final week before a fight"},{t:"The godfather of conditioning for MMA (#131) — The Mayn Idea Podcast",u:"https://hrvzone.com/podcasts/mayn-idea-131-joel-jamieson-conditioning",k:"podcast",d:"Jamieson on conditioning grapplers and UFC champions"},{t:"Phil Daru — official site",u:"https://www.phildaru.com/",k:"article",d:"The fight coach's training, consulting and podcast"},{t:"Fight Strength Podcast — Phil Daru (Apple Podcasts)",u:"https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/fight-strength-podcast/id1247212441",k:"podcast",d:"Daru and Macgregor McNair with fighters and coaches"},{t:"Phil Daru on grappling performance (Ep. 3) — Order & Progress",u:"https://seekprogress.com/blogs/news/ep-3-world-class-advice-from-mma-strength-conditioning-expert-phil-daru",k:"podcast",d:"Strength, assessment and breath work for grapplers"},{t:"The Gable method — Dan John (T Nation)",u:"https://archive.t-nation.com/training/the-gable-method/",k:"article",d:"Gable's rule: if it's important, do it every day"},{t:"Physiology of successful MMA athletes review — Sports Medicine",u:"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26993133/",k:"study",d:"What separates top strikers, grapplers and MMA fighters"},{t:"Physical profiles of Brazilian jiu-jitsu athletes — Sports Medicine Open",u:"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5306420/",k:"study",d:"Strength, power and endurance in jiu-jitsu competitors"}],related:["us-gable-ethic","br-rickson-method","ir-session","cc-chidaoba-train"]}
